	\section{Data Preprocessing}
	\subsection{ Data Cleaning}
	\begin{enumerate}
		\renewcommand{\labelenumi}{\roman{enumi}.}
		\item Removing Null or Empty Rows:\\
		Null values or blank text fields cannot be used for training so rows where the article
		text or label is missing are removed. It ensures the model only sees valid training
		samples.
		\item Removing Duplicate Entries:\\
		Duplicate news articles can bias the model and cause overfitting because the same
		sentence appears multiple times. Due to duplicates entries model memorizes text
		instead of learning patterns. So, we remove duplicates to make the dataset balanced
		and fair.
		\item Irrelevant column elimination:\\
		Columns that do not contribute to the classification task were removed from the
		dataset. These typically include metadata such as URLs, timestamps, authors, or
		other identifiers that are not relevant to the textual content. Eliminating such
		12 columns reduces noise, simplifies the dataset, and ensures that the classification
		model focuses only on meaningful textual features.
		\item HTML Tag Removal:\\
		HTML tag removal means cleaning text that contains HTML formatting symbols
		like <p>, <div>, <br>, <b>, etc. These tags appear when text is copied from
		webpages, blogs, CMS, online articles, or exported documents. Even we don’t
		scrape the data, such tags still come along with the content, so we remove them to
		make the text clean and readable.
		
		Before removing:"<p>{\nepalifont नेपाल राम्रो देश हो} </p>"\\
		After removing:"{\nepalifont नेपाल राम्रो देश हो}"\\
		\item {Unicode Normalization:}\\
		{\nepalifont
			Nepali text may contain multiple Unicode representations of the same character.
			For example, some characters appear as a combined symbol while others appear as
			two separate Unicode points like ``क़'' and ``क'' + ``़''.
		}
		\par
		Before normalization: {\nepalifont क + ़}
		\par
		After normalization: {\nepalifont क़}
		\par
		So, normalization converts all variations into one unified, standard form.
		It prevents treating similar words as different and reduces duplicates in vocabulary.
		\item Whitespace Removal:\\
		Whitespace removal means deleting unnecessary spaces, tabs, or line breaks from
		text. Extra spaces can cause errors in tokenization, matching, and text processing,
		so removing them makes the text more consistent and well-formatted
		
		Before removing:\nepalifont " नेपाल राम्रो छ "\\
		After removing:\nepalifont "नेपाल राम्रो छ"
		\\
		\item Handling special characters:\\
		Special characters such as symbols, emojis, and punctuation marks that do not
		contribute to the news classification task were removed from the text. This step
		helps reduce noise in the dataset, ensures cleaner tokenization, and allows the
		model to focus on meaningful textual content.
		
		\item Stopword removal:\\
		NepBERTa is built on top of the BERT architecture, which use contextual
		embeddings that understand the role of every word in a sentence. Common Nepali
		words such as को, ले, कक, र, मा, or पकन which are considered stopwords in nepali actually
		provide important grammatical and semantic information. Removing them may
		distort the meaning of the sentence, which can reduce model accuracy.\\
		Original sentence: "प्रधानमन्त्रीलेसंसदमा प्रस्ताव पेश गरे।"\\
		After removing stopwords: "प्रधानमन्त्री संसदमा प्रस्ताव पेश गरे"\\
		In above example, sentence loses important context about who performed the
		action.
		
	\end{enumerate}
