		News categories were encoded into numerical labels for model training. The dataset was divided into training, validation, and test sets to enable proper evaluation and avoid overfitting.
		\item Model Selection and Architecture Design\\
		A transformer-based architecture inspired by RoBERTa (NepBERTa) was selected for the feature extraction and a DNN was implemented for classification.
		\item Model Training and Optimization\\
		The model was trained with the help of PyTorch with appropriate loss functions and optimizers. Techniques such as class weighting, early stopping, and learning rate scheduling were applied to improve generalization and handle class imbalance.
		\item Performance Evaluation\\
		The trained model was evaluated using metrics such as accuracy, precision, recall, and F1-score. Detailed classification reports were generated to analyze category-wise performance.
